; Before the first description there is nothing to refresh.
> (raised (lambda () (help:refresh)))
(help:refresh "no description")
; *Help* is made by the first description, in help:mode, with the lighter
; Help, whose hook runs; it keeps no undo history and never reads as
; modified.
> (define notes (buffers:make "notes" "harpo:honk\n"))
> (layout:switch-to-buffer notes)
> (modes:set-major-mode harpo:mode notes)
> (define hooked 0)
> (add-hook! help:mode-hook (lambda () (set! hooked (+ hooked 1))))
> (press! "C-h" "m")
> (list hooked (modes:major-mode (help-buffer)) (modes:lighter help:mode) (buffers:silent? (help-buffer)) (buffers:modified? (help-buffer)))
(1 help:mode "Help" #t #f)
; C-h m: the minor modes on in the view, each with its lighter, its
; documentation and its keymap's; then the major mode and its ancestry.
; Bindings are each keymap's own, walking keymaps bound as prefixes.
> (help)
# Modes
## a minor mode
Whether a buffer's faces are set, so a user can read a buffer in one colour. Its highlighting job runs either way.
## harpo:mode
Its lighter is Harpo.
Harpo's keys.
[C-c h]  <harpo:honk>
> (table-set! modes:minor-modes harpo:horn-mode? 10)
> (table-set! modes:keymaps harpo:horn-mode? harpo:minor-keymap)
> (table-set! modes:lighters harpo:horn-mode? "Horn")
> (keys:bind! harpo:keymap "C-c p" harpo:minor-keymap)
> (press! "C-h" "m")
> (help)
# Modes
## a minor mode
Whether a buffer's faces are set, so a user can read a buffer in one colour. Its highlighting job runs either way.
## Horn
Whether the horn is out.
Keys of the horn mode.
[C-c q]  <harpo:quiet>
## harpo:mode
Its lighter is Harpo.
Harpo's keys.
[C-c h]        <harpo:honk>
[C-c p C-c q]  <harpo:quiet>
; C-h b: one section per active keymap, in lookup order, headed by its
; mode, keys:global, or its documentation; a sequence an earlier keymap
; decides is not listed again.
> (press! "C-h" "b")
> (outline)
# Key bindings
## Horn
## harpo:mode
## The layout's keymap, last on the focus path and for mouse keys on the layout's own drawing.
## keys:global
> (help-with "C-c h]" "C-c q]" "C-c p" "C-x h]" "[C-x C-f]")
[C-c q]  <harpo:quiet>
[C-c h]        <harpo:honk>
[C-c p C-c q]  <harpo:quiet>
[C-x h]            <editing:mark-whole-buffer>
[C-x C-f]          <file-picker:find-file>
; Going back, going forward and refreshing describe from the view first
; described, not from *Help*.
> (layout:select! (help-view))
> (press! "C-h" "m")
> (outline)
# Modes
## a minor mode
## Horn
## help:mode
## modes:special
> (press! "l")
> (help-with "C-c h]" "help:back")
[C-c h]        <harpo:honk>
> (press! "l")
> (title)
"Modes"
> (press! "l")
> (press! "l")
! help:back: no earlier description
> (press! "r")
> (help-with "C-c p")
[C-c p C-c q]  <harpo:quiet>
> (press! "r" "r" "r")
! help:forward: no later description
> (outline)
# Modes
## a minor mode
## Horn
## help:mode
## modes:special
> (press! "g")
> (outline)
# Modes
## a minor mode
## Horn
## help:mode
## modes:special
; A view that is gone gives way to the selected view.
> (press! "l" "l")
> (title)
"Modes"
> (define described (car (views:showing notes)))
> (layout:select! described)
> (press! "C-x" "3" "C-x" "0")
> (list (memq described (views:showing notes)) (length (views:showing notes)))
(#f 1)
> (layout:select! (help-view))
> (press! "g")
> (outline)
